# Nancy CVE suppression file — one entry per line, format: CVE-ID until=YYYY-MM-DD
# Lines starting with # are comments.  Entries expire automatically on the until= date;
# once lapsed the scan fails again, forcing a re-review.
#
# Policy: only suppress a CVE in one of two cases:
#   1. No fixed upstream release exists, so the finding is unactionable.  The entry
#      documents why bumping is not possible.
#   2. The scanner database is wrong: the installed version provably contains the
#      fix.  The entry cites the fix commit, proof that the installed release
#      contains it, and at least two other databases (OSV, Trivy, govulncheck) that
#      report the version clean.  Expiry is at most 30 days.
# Every entry must name the affected package.  Re-check each entry when the weekly dependency scan
# runs (dependency-pin-check.yml / refresh-pins skill) or when a new release of the
# affected package appears.

# CVE-2026-56860 — golang.org/x/net
# Affected package : golang.org/x/net v0.58.0 (indirect dependency)
# Reason           : v0.58.0 is the newest release published upstream as of 2026-08-15;
#                    there is no patched version to upgrade to.  `go list -m -versions
#                    golang.org/x/net` ends at v0.58.0.  Re-check when a newer release
#                    appears or when this entry lapses on the expiry date below.
# Expiry           : 2026-11-15 — after this date the scan re-opens automatically.
CVE-2026-56860 until=2026-11-15

# CVE-2026-84445 — google.golang.org/grpc (scanner database error, policy case 2)
# Affected package : google.golang.org/grpc v1.84.0 (direct dependency)
# Reason           : Sonatype still lists v1.84.0 as affected; the fix is in it.
#                    The fix is grpc-go PR #9365 ("transport: reject requests
#                    missing :authority and host headers"), cherry-picked to the
#                    v1.84.x branch as commit d5a41119e0e3 (#9370). GitHub's
#                    compare d5a41119e0e3...v1.84.0 reports status=ahead,
#                    ahead_by=3, behind_by=0: the v1.84.0 tag contains the fix.
#                    OSV GO-2026-6443 (corrected 2026-10-07) lists the 1.84.0-dev
#                    range as fixed at 1.84.0-dev.0.20260825144003-d5a41119e0e3,
#                    so v1.84.0 is unaffected. Trivy (0 HIGH/CRITICAL) and
#                    govulncheck v1.7.0, linux and GOOS=windows (0 affecting)
#                    agree, measured 2026-10-13 on PR #4971.
# Expiry           : 2026-11-13 — if Sonatype still flags it then, re-check.
CVE-2026-84445 until=2026-11-13
